---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Komadrona Review handles browser-local progress, attempts, bookmarks, application storage, hosting logs, and voluntary contact."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Version 1 privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>Version 1 is designed to avoid creating a centralized learner profile, score database, or account system.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="container prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Learning data stays local, but local does not mean indestructible</strong>
      <p>
        Acknowledgments, lesson progress, bookmarks, quiz attempts, selected answers, scores, and related study records
        are designed to remain in browser storage on the learner's device. Clearing site data, using private browsing,
        reinstalling the browser or application, resetting the device, changing browsers, or moving to another device
        may permanently remove them. Komadrona Review has no central learner backup and cannot restore deleted records.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What the application does not request</h2>
    <p>Komadrona Review Version 1 does not provide accounts and does not require the learner to submit:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>a name, school, student number, professional license number, phone number, or home address;</li>
      <li>an email address to read lessons or take in-app practice questions;</li>
      <li>a quiz screenshot, score report, identification document, or educational record; or</li>
      <li>health information, patient information, or clinical records.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information stored in the browser</h2>
    <p>
      Small application preferences and acknowledgments may be stored through browser local storage. Structured learner
      data such as quiz attempts, selected answers, scores, bookmarks, lesson progress, and storage metadata is designed
      for IndexedDB. Offline application files may later use service-worker Cache Storage when the installable offline
      release is implemented.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current practice-engine preview already stores completed fixture attempts and question bookmarks in IndexedDB.
      These records are not intentionally submitted to a Komadrona learner server.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browser storage can be inspected, changed, exported, imported, or deleted by a person with access to the device.
      It must not be treated as a secure record, an official grade, proof of identity, or evidence of examination
      eligibility or readiness.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage persistence and backups</h2>
    <p>
      The application may ask the browser to grant persistent storage. The browser decides whether to grant that request,
      and the learner can still delete the data manually. Persistent-storage status therefore does not replace backups.
    </p>
    <p>
      Export and import are required before learner progress is considered recoverable. Until those controls are
      implemented and tested, local progress must be treated as disposable study data.
    </p>

    <h2>In-app questions and scores</h2>
    <p>
      Practice questions are delivered as part of the Komadrona application instead of through an external quiz
      provider. Answer checking, rationales, bookmarks, scoring, and attempt history are intended to run locally in the
      browser. No score submission, screenshot submission, or server-side learner profile is required.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because question content and answer keys are delivered to the learner's device, the practice system is not a
      secure or proctored examination. It is a private study tool only.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and technical records</h2>
    <p>
      The application is planned for static hosting through Vercel. Like ordinary hosting providers, Vercel may process
      technical request, network, security, and diagnostic information needed to deliver and protect the service.
      Komadrona Review does not use those provider records to create learner score profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>Voluntary communication</h2>
    <p>
      When a user voluntarily contacts the maintainer to report an error, copyright concern, security problem, or
      source suggestion, the maintainer receives the contact details and message supplied by that user. Such messages
      should not include patient information, examination leaks, government identifiers, or unnecessary personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics, advertising, and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Version 1 does not intentionally include Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, advertising trackers, behavioral
      profiling tools, or embedded social-media widgets. A later change that introduces analytics or centralized data
      collection must first update this notice and the project's technical documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy principles</h2>
    <p>
      Where personal information is processed through voluntary communication or future features, the project intends
      to apply transparency, a specified legitimate purpose, proportionality, data minimization, reasonable security,
      and limited retention consistent with applicable Philippine privacy requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
    <p>
      A dedicated project contact address will be published before public release. Until then, privacy concerns may be
      raised through the repository's GitHub issue process without posting sensitive personal information publicly.
    </p>

    <p class="small-print">Effective date: 4 August 2026. Applies to Komadrona Review Version 1.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
